This is not exactly the same as the definition in Hartshorne. Namely, the definition in Hartshorne (8th corrected printing, 1997) is that $f$ should be the composition of an open immersion followed by a H-projective morphism (see Definition <a href="/tag/01W8" data-tag="01W8">29.44.1</a>), which does not imply $f$ is quasi-compact. See Lemma <a href="/tag/01WA" data-tag="01WA">29.44.11</a> for the implication in the other direction.